Found it. Commit b83ce94c6 merged the correct if/else-if (with separate `CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_COMBAT` sound and separate `m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove = true` assignment) into a single combined `if` condition using OR logic, which dropped the `m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove = true` assignment for the combat branch and always played `CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_NONCOMBAT` regardless of combat/non-combat. The fixing commit 9a02e14e1 essentially reverts this by splitting back into two separate `if` blocks (though it left the wrong sound path `CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_NONCOMBAT` for the combat case, a separate minor issue not part of this bug's fix scope).

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: b83ce94c63ec1891f5b76837455c8b2a53ad9d9c

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I traced the file history of `TripleAPlayer.java` using `git log -S "m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove"` to find commits that touched the relevant flag, then inspected each candidate diff with `git show`.

**(2) Root cause:** Commit `b83ce94c6` (Sep 18, 2015) refactored the sound-playing logic for the move phase. Before it, the code was:
```java
if (nonCombat && !m_soundPlayedAlreadyNonCombatMove) {
    ...play CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_NONCOMBAT...
    m_soundPlayedAlreadyNonCombatMove = true;
} else if (!nonCombat && !m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove) {
    ...play CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_COMBAT...
    m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove = true;
}
```
This commit collapsed it into:
```java
if ((nonCombat && !m_soundPlayedAlreadyNonCombatMove) || (!nonCombat && !m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove)) {
    ClipPlayer.play(SoundPath.CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_NONCOMBAT, id.getName());
    m_soundPlayedAlreadyNonCombatMove = true;
}
```
This single-branch merge is the bug: for the combat-move case (`!nonCombat`), `m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove` is never set to `true`, so the "already played" guard never engages — the combat-move sound would replay on every invocation instead of once per game. It also incorrectly plays the non-combat clip in the combat case (a pre-existing/adjacent issue not corrected until later).

**(3) Evidence:** The fixing commit `9a02e14e1` directly restores separate `if` blocks and re-adds `m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove = true;`, which is precisely the assignment that `b83ce94c6` removed. This is a clean, high-confidence match — the fix is structurally the inverse of the introducing change.

